{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Blessed of sons be Asher.</b> I saw in the books — there is no tribe among all the tribes that was blessed with sons like Asher, and I do not know how." "<b>Let him be the delight of his brothers.</b> That he would ingratiate himself to his brothers with oil drawn from anpikinon and with flasks, and they would ingratiate themselves to him with produce. Another interpretation — <b>let him be the delight of his brothers</b> — that his daughters were beautiful, and this is what is said in Chronicles (1 Chronicles 7) ״he was the father of Birzaith,״ for his daughters were married to high priests and kings who are anointed with olive oil." "<b>And let him dip his foot in oil.</b> That his land would draw oil like a fountain. And an incident: the people of Laodicea needed oil, they appointed for them a certain Pulmostus, etc., as is found in Menachot (85b)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {1 "אַנְפִּיקִינוֹן is an Aramaic borrowing from Greek amphikellon, a wine-oil flask; kept transliterated as Rashi's source-term."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:53.740838179Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}